DOCKER SWARM:

High availability: deploying the app on more than one server
means using the cluster.

Docker Swarm is a container orchestration tool.
It is used to manage multiple containers on multiple nodes.
Each node will have a copy of a single container.
Here we have manager and worker nodes.
The manager node will create containers and send them to the worker nodes.
worker nodes will take the container and manage it.
The manager node communicates with the worker node by using a token.

SETUP:
1. Create 3 servers (1=manager, 2=worker) (all traffic must)
yum install docker -y
systemctl start docker
systemctl status docker

2. Set the hostnames:
hostnamectl set-hostname manager/worker-1/worker-2

3. generate and copy token:
manager node: docker swarm init
Copy the token to all worker nodes

